# Repo-owned security-review scope: this repo's security-sensitive surfaces.
# Two readers, one list:
# - the ci-workflows claude-security-review reusable workflow, via its
#   `paths-file` input, reads it from the PR's BASE branch. An absent file
#   FAILS OPEN (every PR reviewed); a forbidden pattern fails the lane closed.
# - the LOCAL security review on the operator's session, through the
#   `security` rule of the `pr_skill_evidence` key in
#   .claude/source-control.md, which cites it as
#   `@file:.github/claude-security-paths`.
# The breadth below is what makes both fire on nearly every non-docs pull
# request, which is deliberate.
# Format: gitignore patterns (one per line), matched via `git check-ignore`
# from the repo root; `!`, `?`, and `+` are forbidden. `#` comments and blank
# lines are ignored.
.github/**
.claude/**
scripts/**
plugins/*/hooks/**
plugins/*/bin/**
plugins/*/tools/**
plugins/*/skills/**
plugins/*/agents/**
plugins/*/commands/**
.claude-plugin/**
REVIEW.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
plugins/*/src/**
plugins/*/dist/**
**/*.sh
**/*.ps1
**/*.mjs
**/*.ts
**/*.js
**/*.cjs
**/.mcp.json
**/mcp.json
**/package.json
**/package-lock.json
plugins/*/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
